Patch T7 libm (rung 1b, task T7): keep libm's soft-float code in the core
set now that wgpu is in the workspace. This is architecture.toml's part of
the fix; t7-eng-gpu.patch holds the rest.

Why: wgpu's shader compiler, naga, depends on half with its num-traits
feature; half turns on num-traits' libm feature, and num-traits takes libm
with its default features, which include `arch`. Cargo unifies features
across the workspace, so with wgpu in it, every workspace build compiles
the simulation's libm with `arch`, and arch-check fails with [E-ARCH-PIN].
naga needs that half feature, so no choice of crates avoids it.

The fix: eng-math gives libm `force-soft-floats` (the root Cargo.toml's
`[workspace.dependencies]`, in t7-eng-gpu.patch). libm 0.2.16 compiles its
`arch` code only for `arch` without `force-soft-floats` (configure.rs), and
outside it has no arch-specific code but i586's, so libm compiles exactly
as it does today with no features, whatever turns `arch` on. This patch
pins the workspace's resulting set, ["arch", "default",
"force-soft-floats"]. Builds of the core set alone (RISC-V, wasm32)
resolve to `force-soft-floats` only and compile the same code. Losing
`force-soft-floats` fails the pin.

Checked: the hash streams are unchanged (`cargo xtask replay`, no
`--regen`). T7's `reviewer` subagent read libm 0.2.16's configure.rs and
math/arch independently and confirmed that the fix changes no simulation
result.

Apply it with t7-eng-gpu.patch, in one commit: arch-check fails with
either alone. Base: main at 31c3a8c. It touches architecture.toml only, so
it does not depend on the G3 patch or on t6-oracles.patch. At the repo
root, run `git apply` with this file, then with t7-eng-gpu.patch, then
`cargo xtask quick`. Session 17's T7 entry in PROGRESS.md says how it was
tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

diff --git a/architecture.toml b/architecture.toml
index 20c4d3b7501da545ddb199f8dadf4bf2ded0173f..67971bbc769ff2b2a46ae9331df6bc8a2d15a8cd 100644
--- a/architecture.toml
+++ b/architecture.toml
@@ -13,8 +13,12 @@ allowed_patches = []
 # Third-party crates the core set may reach, transitively, pinned to an exact
 # version from crates.io and an exact feature set. eng-derive is a
 # proc-macro: its syn/quote/proc-macro2 dependencies are build-time only.
+# libm's set is the workspace's: wgpu's shader compiler, naga, turns on
+# libm's default `arch` feature (through half and num-traits), and eng-math's
+# `force-soft-floats` switches its code back off. The core set's math is then
+# the same in every build, with or without eng-gpu (rung 1b, T7).
 [core_third_party]
-libm = { version = "0.2.16", features = [] }
+libm = { version = "0.2.16", features = ["arch", "default", "force-soft-floats"] }
 
 # Floor crates and the single engine crate allowed to depend on each.
 [floor]
